Trained model weights and derived data
=====================================

Files: web/model.json, docs/demo/model.json, experiments/**/*.pt, data/processed/**, data/splits/**

These were trained on, or derived from, the datasets released with

  Peter O'Donovan, Aseem Agarwala, Aaron Hertzmann.
  "Color Compatibility From Large Datasets." ACM Transactions on Graphics 30(4), SIGGRAPH 2011.
  https://www.dgp.toronto.edu/~donovan/color/

  Peter O'Donovan, Aseem Agarwala, Aaron Hertzmann.
  "Collaborative Filtering of Color Aesthetics." Computational Aesthetics (CAe) 2014.
  https://www.dgp.toronto.edu/~donovan/cfcolor/

which the authors distribute under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 2.5 Canada
license (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/2.5/ca/).

Accordingly, the weights and derived data in this repository are released under
CC BY-NC-SA 2.5 Canada. You may use, share and adapt them for noncommercial purposes,
with attribution to the original authors above and to this repository, and any
adaptation must carry the same license. Commercial use is not permitted.

The raw datasets themselves are not redistributed here; download them from the project pages above.
Verified counts, checksums and the license notices as they appeared are recorded in data/manifest/.

The Sanzo Wada palettes (data/processed/wada.parquet, if built) come from Matt DesLauriers' MIT-licensed
transcription (https://github.com/mattdesl/dictionary-of-colour-combinations); the U.S. copyright status of
the underlying 1933-34 work is unresolved and they are not included in the trained weights.
